    "title": "BAKER/POWDER VALLEY BASEBALL: Bulldogs roll past Nyssa, 14-3 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jayson Jaco ,\n21 hours ago Baker's Jake McClaughry takes a swing against Enterprise/Joseph/Wallowa on April 22, 2025. (Jayson Jacoby/Baker City Herald) The Baker/Powder Valley baseball team took the lead with a 5-run second inning and went on to rout Nyssa 14-3 in five innings in a nonleague game Tuesday, May 19, at the Baker Sports Complex.\nTucker Reid was 4 for 4, and Jake McClaughry 3 for 4 with a triple and two RBIs. Ethan Rayl and Clay Stevens were both 2 for 3 with two RBIs. Gerik Orszulak was 2 for 2 with an RBI and earned the win on the mound, striking out four in 3.1 innings. Will O’Connell pitched the final 1.2 innings. Baker had 16 hits to Nyssa’s four.\nBaker wraps up the regular season by hosting Ontario on Thursday, May 21, in a doubleheader starting at 2 p.m.\nBaker swept the Tigers on May 1 at Ontario.\nAlthough the Bulldogs, with a 2-8 record, can’t earn one of the Greater Oregon League’s two automatic playoff berths, Baker still has a chance for one of the four at-large bids.\nThe four highest ranked third-place teams also qualify for the playoffs.\nAs of Wednesday morning, Baker, ranked 22nd, was the fifth-highest third-place team. Astoria, ranked 17th, would be the final playoff team based on the current rankings.",
    "summary": "17 hours ago Baker's Jake McClaughry takes a swing against Enterprise/Joseph/Wallowa on April 22, 2025. (Jayson Jacoby/Baker City Herald) The Baker/Powder Valley baseball team took the lead with a 5-run second inning and went on to rout Nyssa 14-3 in five innings in a nonleague game Tuesday, May 19, at the Baker Sports Complex. Gerik Orszulak was 2 for 2 with an RBI and earned the win on the mound, striking out four in 3.1 innings.",
